      "summary": "Reynier's leading division, which reached Großbeeren in the rain about four in the afternoon, drove out the Prussian battalion holding it, and occupied the village. At six Bülow's whole corps came on behind sixty guns; the Saxons fought in the burning village with the bayonet and the musket butt until they were driven out.",
